# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# v1.0.79, opened by scripts/new_cut.sh from v1.0.78.
#
# WHY THESE PINS:
#   v1.0.79 is the FIRST cut since v1.0.77 with a changed payload, and both 
#   changes exist because the v1.0.78 cold walk could finally see them. CM051 
#   #1848 creates the qdrant collections where store readiness is PROVEN 
#   rather than on a one-shot 300s cap, and re-checks PER NAME because a 
#   cardinality test cannot see a missing member; it closes a RECURRENCE that 
#   install.sh:29350 already records from the v1.0.60 walk. CM051 #1850 
#   re-arms the store curl credential after the promote: the array was armed 
#   with -K into the /tmp staging tree, promote deleted that tree, and every 
#   later credentialed curl exited 26 against a store that answered 9971 
#   times with 200. CM051 #1849 is harness-only and makes the walk wait for 
#   each people store to STOP MOVING before the two reconcile probes run, 
#   gating on per-store stability rather than on the two stores agreeing, 
#   which would have been a fixture. DAEMON_COMMIT is unchanged at e3ddf5de 
#   (hub-v0.4.75, tarball b2e58127), so no daemon rebuild is involved and the 
#   Q1 grounded FAIL is expected to remain. This cut is NOT a CLEAN 
#   candidate: three FAIL rows are predicted in cut-manifests/v1.0.79.yaml 
#   before the tag.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
